  "steps": [
    "Explicit clip usage reads only saved same-scene behaviors. Four complete UUID parameters match in author order; embedded prose is excluded. The local renamed form, reviewed proposal and active animation clock remain intact. No author files or source draft change.",
    "Readonly saved-source navigation selects the second binding exact parameter token, not an earlier identical ID in prose. BOM/CRLF source is displayed with browser newline normalization only. At390px Chinese/English/Japanese retain the textarea node, focus, caret, scroll and active preview, with footer controls reachable. Cancel preserves original draft and every author file.",
    "An unavailable usage service preserves reviewed animation and active playback. Retry succeeds; subsequent reads keep an incomplete numeric field, original node and selection unchanged.",
    "Switching clips while a saved reply is held rejects the old result; closing and reopening rejects the previous session. Neither response fills or reopens the wrong usage panel.",
    "A fixture-controlled newly allocated UUID can be checked before the clip is saved: the panel filters existing saved future-parameter matches, labels the clip as current-form data and performs no write.",
    "Removing a referenced clip clears its usage/source view and invalidates the detached source button. Usage is advisory and does not block review: Apply changes only the ordinary draft; Save persists the exact reviewed BOM/CRLF animation. Saved behaviors and every other author file remain byte-identical."
  ],
